WEBVTT

NOTE On-screen visual text only; this approved video has no audio track.

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:07.350
AI is the broad set; it includes rule-based systems and systems that learn.

2
00:00:07.350 --> 00:00:14.200
Machine learning learns from data. Deep learning uses neural networks with multiple layers.

3
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:21.550
Generating content describes a purpose: deep networks can also classify, not only generate.

4
00:00:22.050 --> 00:00:28.900
We test whether the sensor reading exceeds four units.

5
00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:35.750
Training compares that split with another at six units.

6
00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:43.800
This example selects six because it separates these labels, not because six is a physical law.

7
00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:51.150
The word urgent appears in eight of ten spam messages in this example.

8
00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:58.000
It also appears in one of ten legitimate messages.

9
00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.350
These are class-conditional frequencies; a posterior also needs priors and other evidence.

10
00:01:05.850 --> 00:01:12.700
A group contains three points at horizontal coordinates one, three and five.

11
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:19.550
Its current center is at two; recomputing the mean moves it to three.

12
00:01:19.550 --> 00:01:26.900
The new center depends on cluster assignments, not on an external label.

13
00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:35.317
Two inputs, two weights: two times zero point four minus zero point two gives zero point six.

14
00:01:35.317 --> 00:01:42.167
ReLU keeps this positive value. Against target one, squared error is zero point sixteen.

15
00:01:42.167 --> 00:01:49.517
Training uses that error to adjust weights; inference uses the weights already fixed.

16
00:01:50.017 --> 00:01:56.867
Initial evaluation uses readings similar to the training data.

17
00:01:56.867 --> 00:02:03.717
Later the input distribution changes while the model remains identical.

18
00:02:03.717 --> 00:02:11.767
Detected drift calls for checking performance; drift alone does not prove every prediction is wrong.

